# Generated, committed artifacts whose form carries WHOLE-FILE state — content
# hashes and tallies — and which are therefore REGENERATED, never merged
# (issue #3069).
#
# The `regenerated` driver runs the ordinary 3-way merge first and keeps a clean
# result; only on a genuine conflict does it take ours and mark the path, and
# `scripts/resolve-generated-artifacts.ts` re-derives it once at the rebased tip.
#
# The driver itself lives in LOCAL git config (it cannot be committed) and is
# registered by `bun run worktree:init`. Without that registration git falls
# back to the default text merge, i.e. exactly the behaviour that predates this
# file — a missing bootstrap degrades, it does not corrupt.
#
# This list is not hand-maintained: `scripts/__tests__/generated-artifact-merge.test.ts`
# pins it to REGENERATED_ARTIFACTS in `scripts/lib/generated-artifacts.ts`,
# which also records why every OTHER script-written committed artifact is out
# of the class — a new generator classifies its output there (issue #6116).
data/oracle-compiled.json merge=regenerated
data/oracle-legality.json merge=regenerated
data/catalogue/source-hash.json merge=regenerated
data/catalogue/packed-corpus.json merge=regenerated
data/catalogue/definition-index.json merge=regenerated
data/catalogue/search-index.json merge=regenerated
data/blade-card-index.json merge=regenerated
data/blade-reproducers.json merge=regenerated
AGENTS.md merge=regenerated
convex/AGENTS.md merge=regenerated
src/AGENTS.md merge=regenerated

# Committed artifacts that are NOT re-derivable — so out of the class above —
# but whose conflicts are still never a real disagreement (issue #3768). Each
# carries its OWN driver, which resolves the file semantically and leaves
# nothing to regenerate at the rebased tip. Pinned to OTHER_MERGE_DRIVERS by
# the same test, and registered by the same `bun run worktree:init`.
data/cr/citations-ledger.json merge=cr-ledger

# The issue-log ratchet baseline (issue #6276): a sorted key set that only
# shrinks. Adjacent or overlapping deletions on two branches conflict as text
# without disagreeing; the `key-set` driver merges it as a set.
data/issue-log-comments-baseline.json merge=key-set

# Hand-written append-only lists (issue #5942): two branches appending an entry
# at the same end conflict without disagreeing. The `append-only` driver merges
# in diff3 style and concatenates only the hunks where both sides purely
# inserted; any hunk touching an existing line stays a conflict. (git's built-in
# `union` is NOT that: it keeps lines both sides share once, fusing two appended
# entries into one object.) Pinned to OTHER_MERGE_DRIVERS by the same test and
# registered by the same `bun run worktree:init`.
convex/gre/ai/blade/scenarios.ts merge=append-only
convex/oracle/grammar/fixtures.ts merge=append-only
